                    <death when="1000-12-31"/>
                    <occupation>Lawyer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Attorney at Law, FAS, Great Winchester Street, London, and a contributor
                            to charities including those for the education of the children of the respectably
                            destitute. He is noted as the Attorney in cases of bankrupcy - for
                            example, A. Heurtley, Merchant noted in 5 June 1815; or W. Humble 10
                            October, 1815. Also author of 'The American Encroachment of British
                            Rights', in The Pamphleteer No XI and XII 1815; and Founder of the Pitt Club</p>.
                        <p>Features in a fraud case, where he is the intended victim, in August 1816. </p>
                        <p>Almost certainly involved in Godwin's financial affairs.</p>
                    </note>
                   
